---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Mark from '../../components/Mark.astro';
import '../../styles/detail.css';
const mailto = "mailto:manuel@triarc.ch?subject=Recruiting%20%E2%80%93%20enquiry&body=Business%3A%0APosition%3A%0AStart%20date%3A%0A";
const urgentMail = "mailto:manuel@triarc.ch?subject=Cover%20at%20short%20notice%20%E2%80%93%20urgent&body=Business%3A%0APosition%20lost%3A%0AFrom%20when%20and%20how%20long%3A%0A";
---
<Base
  title="Recruiting for hospitality & hotels | Triarc"
  description="Cover at short notice for head-of roles — head chef, front office manager, chef patissier, general management: ask today, 48 hours later a working professional from our worldwide network takes over. Plus the permanent side: head-of roles and every position in the house — kitchen, service, front and back office, housekeeping, patisserie, maintenance."
  lang="en"
  crumb="Recruiting"
  altHref="/recruiting"
  hreflang={{ de: '/recruiting', en: '/en/recruiting' }}
>
  <main id="main" class="detail" style="--accent: var(--gold); --accent-wash: color-mix(in srgb, var(--gold) 7%, transparent);">
    <section class="instrument-hero">
      <div>
        <Mark size={76} />
        <p class="d-eyebrow"><span class="roman">III</span>People &amp; placement</p>
        <h1 class="d-h1">Recruiting<span class="stop">.</span></h1>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Service III of III</p>
        <p class="role">Covered.<br />The day after tomorrow, too.</p>
        <p class="hero-intro">A head-of role drops out — head chef, front office manager, chef patissier, general management — or a gap opens until the next hire who can only start in three months? We hold the line: ask today — <strong>48 hours later</strong> an experienced professional from our international network, matched to your operation, takes over and supports the team until it is steady again. Alongside that, the permanent side: head-of roles and every position in the house — kitchen, service, front and back office, housekeeping, patisserie, maintenance. Whatever post is open.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="btn" href={mailto}>Discuss a position <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <a class="btn-ghost" href="#cover">Cover at short notice</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="trust-strip">
      <span class="who">Placed by <strong>Manuel Bänziger</strong></span>
      <span class="items"><span>Executive chef &amp; F&amp;B leader</span><span>20+ years international</span><span>Worldwide network of working professionals</span><span>Led teams from brigade to management</span></span>
    </section>

    <section class="block reveal" id="paths">
      <div class="block-head">
        <h2 class="section-kicker">Two ways</h2>
        <p class="pull">Fill the post — or have someone standing there tomorrow.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="options">
        <article class="option">
          <div class="accent-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="opt-eyebrow"><span class="roman">A</span>Permanent placement</p>
          <h3 class="opt-name">Recruiting<span class="stop">.</span></h3>
          <p class="opt-role">The right person, not the quickest one.</p>
          <p class="opt-body">Head-of roles and every position in the house — kitchen, service, front and back office, housekeeping, patisserie, maintenance — vetted by someone who has filled and led those posts himself. A few candidates instead of a stack of CVs, then a settling-in period we stay close to. We take the time a permanent hire deserves.</p>
          <a class="opt-link" href={mailto}>Discuss a position</a>
        </article>
        <article class="option urgent">
          <div class="accent-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="opt-eyebrow"><span class="roman">B</span>Head-of roles · emergency</p>
          <h3 class="opt-name">Cover at short notice<span class="stop">.</span></h3>
          <p class="opt-role">Someone is there within 48 hours. Guaranteed.</p>
          <p class="opt-body">The head chef drops out, the front office manager resigns mid-season, the chef patissier is gone for weeks — and the next hire cannot start for three months. For head-of roles. A working professional from our worldwide network takes the post — and stays until your team stands again. Or until you have calmly found the right person: we buy you the time for that.</p>
          <a class="opt-link" href={urgentMail}>Request cover</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="split reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Why us</p>
        <p class="pull">A CV doesn’t tell you who holds a Friday night.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="founder-line">Leaving a post open costs you. Filling it wrong costs three times over: in the hire, in the knowledge that walks back out of the house, and in the offboarding — plus the search that starts again from scratch.</p>
        <p class="body">Most hospitality recruiters have never stood in a kitchen. They check the stations on a CV and hope it fits — you find out in the first service whether it does.</p>
        <p class="body">We have held and staffed those posts ourselves. <strong>We know which question separates people in an interview</strong>, who carries the pressure and who only talks about it — and we know the difference between a forty-cover room and a banquet for four hundred — or four thousand.</p>
        <p class="body">And because we also advise operations and build for them, we know the house someone is walking into. Placement then isn’t an address; it’s a fit.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block reveal">
      <div class="block-head">
        <h2 class="section-kicker">What we place</h2>
        <p class="pull">From commis to general management.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cap-grid">
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">01</span><h3>Head-of roles</h3><p>Head chef, sous chef, general management, F&amp;B management. The appointments where a wrong call costs a year — checked accordingly.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">02</span><h3>Kitchen &amp; service</h3><p>Every position in brigade and service, from commis through patisserie to waiting staff and bar.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">03</span><h3>Front &amp; back office</h3><p>Reception, reservations and administration — the posts where the stay begins and the accounting ends.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">04</span><h3>Housekeeping &amp; maintenance</h3><p>Floors, laundry, engineering and upkeep — the departments that carry a house even though no guest ever sees them on the bill.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">05</span><h3>Temporary &amp; seasonal</h3><p>Extra hands and seasonal staff for peaks, banquets and the months when a house does twice the work.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">06</span><h3>Placement + settling in</h3><p>Nobody is dropped in cold: we accompany the first weeks and put new people straight onto the planned rota — in Nova if you like.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">07</span><h3>Cover at short notice</h3><p>For head-of roles — head chef, front office manager, chef patissier, F&amp;B and general management. A working professional takes over within 48 hours and stays until the post is properly filled again.</p></div>
        <div class="cap"><span class="num">08</span><h3>Time for the right hire</h3><p>You do not have to fill a head-of role under pressure: the cover runs the department until you have found the right person — not the first available one.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="nachweis reveal" id="cover">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Cover at short notice</p>
        <h2>Ask today.<br />Someone is there the day after tomorrow.</h2>
        <p>The head chef, the front office manager, the chef patissier, the general manager — when a head-of role drops out, the whole department stalls. The season is running, the next hire cannot start for three months, and the operation cannot wait three months. We hold the line — <strong>within 48 hours, guaranteed</strong>: an experienced professional from our international network, still working in the trade themselves, takes the post and carries your team until it stands again. Not a stopgap — someone who genuinely fills the role.</p>
        <p>And it need not be an emergency at all: often a house simply needs more time to hire properly. <strong>That time is what we buy you</strong> — the cover holds the operation until you have found the right person, instead of taking the first available one under pressure.</p>
        <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:26px"><a class="btn" href={urgentMail}>Request cover <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="doc-list">
          <p class="lbl">Head-of roles we bridge</p>
          <li>Head chef &amp; sous chef</li>
          <li>Front office manager &amp; head of reservations</li>
          <li>Chef patissier &amp; head baker</li>
          <li>F&amp;B manager &amp; restaurant manager</li>
          <li>Head of housekeeping</li>
          <li>General manager &amp; director</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block reveal">
      <h2 class="section-kicker">How it runs</h2>
      <p class="pull">The shape of a placement.</p>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><span class="n">1</span><h3>Understand the house</h3><p>We work out how your operation actually runs — team, kitchen, what the post really demands.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="n">2</span><h3>Introduce</h3><p>You get a few vetted candidates instead of a stack of CVs — with our honest read on each.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="n">3</span><h3>Arrive</h3><p>We stay through the first weeks: settling in, the rota, and a call after the first month.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="assurance">
        <span>A few vetted candidates instead of volume</span>
        <span>An honest read — even when it argues against a placement</span>
        <span>Confidential towards operation and candidate alike</span>
        <span>Head-of roles within 48 hours — guaranteed, available worldwide</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-band reveal">
      <h2>Which position is open?</h2>
      <p>Tell us who you are looking for and from when. If someone has just dropped out, today is the right day — then someone is standing in your operation the day after tomorrow.</p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="justify-content:center"><a class="btn" href={mailto}>Discuss a position <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <p class="contact-line">Direct: <a href="mailto:manuel@triarc.ch">manuel@triarc.ch</a></p>
    </section>

    <nav class="instrument-nav" aria-label="Triarc services">
      <a href="/en/">← Overview</a>
      <div class="links"><a href="/en/software">Software</a><a href="/en/beratung">Consulting</a><a href="/en/recruiting" aria-current="page">Recruiting</a></div>
    </nav>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  /* the service names are longer words than Aurora/Nova/Zenith/Ceres,
     so the display size steps down to keep them inside the column */
  .d-h1 { font-size: clamp(40px, 5.8vw, 74px); }

  /* the two ways in, held apart as a pair: a post to fill, or a hole to close
     today — they are bought for different reasons */
  .options { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 28px; align-items: stretch; }
  .option {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;
    padding: 32px 32px 34px; border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper-deep) 55%, transparent);
    transition: border-color 320ms var(--ease);
  }
  .option:hover { border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--gold) 55%, transparent); }
  .option.urgent { background: var(--accent-wash); }
  .option .accent-rule { width: 100%; height: 2px; background: var(--gold); margin-bottom: 4px; transform: scaleX(0.2); transform-origin: left center; transition: transform 420ms var(--ease); }
  .option:hover .accent-rule { transform: scaleX(1); }
  .opt-eyebrow { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.3em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }
  .opt-eyebrow .roman { color: var(--gold); margin-right: 8px; }
  .opt-name { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 300; font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--ink); margin: 0; }
  .opt-name .stop { color: var(--gold); }
  .opt-role { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-weight: 300; font-size: 18px; color: var(--gold); margin: 0; line-height: 1.3; text-wrap: balance; }
  .opt-body { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.68; color: var(--ink); margin: 2px 0 0; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .opt-link { align-self: flex-start; margin-top: auto; padding: 14px 0 3px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gold); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); transition: color 180ms ease; }
  .opt-link:hover { color: var(--gold); }

  @media (max-width: 820px) { .options { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 22px; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .option, .option .accent-rule { transition: none; } }
</style>
